yaml:
rules:
  - id: dubbo-npe-c1-2-r1
    languages: [java]
    severity: ERROR
    message: >-
      Cache read and populate are nested inside a guard that requires the derived
      cache key to be non-null. When the key is null the cache is neither read nor
      populated, so execution silently falls through to an uncached invocation and
      the cache is defeated. A null key is a perfectly valid cache key: consult and
      populate the cache unconditionally, and guard only on the cache object itself.
    patterns:
      - pattern: |
          if (<... $KEY != null ...>) {
            ...
            $CACHE.get($KEY);
            ...
            $CACHE.put($KEY, ...);
            ...
          }
      # Equivalent guards that validate the key itself (emptiness / length / size)
      # make the cache access correct -- do not flag them.
      - pattern-not-inside: |
          if (<... $KEY.length() ...>) {
            ...
          }
      - pattern-not-inside: |
          if (<... $KEY.isEmpty() ...>) {
            ...
          }
      - pattern-not-inside: |
          if (<... $KEY.size() ...>) {
            ...
          }
